│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ severity_gated_relocation                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ The baseline uses radius_scale=1, fraction=1, memory reevaluation, and retained           │
│                          │ velocities. Its persistent interval-end errors motivate testing broader recovery after    │
│                          │ substantial deterioration.                                                                │
│                          │ This policy maps relative fitness drops of 2–20% to increasing response strength. It      │
│                          │ relocates 40–100% of particles, preserves more particles when the swarm already spans the │
│                          │ response region, and expands the radius up to twice baseline. Velocity resets require     │
│                          │ severe deterioration, little recent improvement, and a compact swarm. Memory reevaluation │
