│ patch_description        │ The current policy maps 2–20% fitness deterioration to radius scales of 0.75–2.0,         │
│                          │ relocates 40–100% of particles, and sometimes resets velocity. Its lower mean error       │
│                          │ accompanies regressions on two cases, so stronger relocation is not consistently          │
│                          │ beneficial.                                                                               │
│                          │ This proposal caps radius scale at 1.5 and relocation fraction at 0.8. Deterioration sets │
│                          │ response strength; recent improvement limits expansion, while existing dispersion reduces │
│                          │ relocation. Memory reevaluation and velocity retention preserve useful search             │
│                          │ information. The hypothesis is that retaining some particles and limiting expansion       │
│                          │ improves recovery without repeatedly disrupting local tracking. Memory refresh costs      │
│                          │ under 1% of evaluations in the supplied feedback, providing little motivation for         │
│                          │ wholesale memory reset. Performance improvement remains to be measured.                   │
