│ patch_description        │ The stronger relocation and velocity reset increased mean error from 2.31 to 2.33 without │
│                          │ resolving the worst case. Remove that escalation and test a different recovery mechanism: │
│                          │ reset memories only when severe deterioration, compact geometry, and stalled progress     │
│                          │ coincide. The hypothesis is that concentrated historical attractors can delay recovery    │
│                          │ after a substantial change; releasing them may help retained particles explore while      │
│                          │ preserving velocity and the parent's bounded relocation radius. Otherwise, reevaluate     │
│                          │ memories to preserve useful search history. Memory refresh consumes less than 1% of       │
│                          │ evaluations, so the intended benefit is improved recovery rather than evaluation savings. │
│                          │ This proposal requires measurement; the existing feedback does not establish memory       │
│                          │ retention as the cause of tracking failure.                                               │
