│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ compact_swarm_recovery_floor                                                              │
│ patch_description        │ Test whether small fitness drops conceal meaningful displacement when a swarm is tightly  │
│                          │ concentrated. Relative fitness loss need not measure how far a peak moved, so the current │
│                          │ narrow response may leave compact swarms searching around an obsolete location.           │
│                          │ For compact swarms, smoothly raise the minimum radius multiplier toward 2.0 and           │
│                          │ relocation fraction toward 0.60, preserving some positional anchors. The extra response   │
│                          │ vanishes when swarm diameter reaches twice the default radius. Stronger existing          │
│                          │ responses remain intact; memory reevaluation and velocity preservation continue.          │
│                          │ The stronger prior program outperformed the conservative policy, while some cases         │
│                          │ retained substantial interval-end error. This motivates testing additional spatial        │
│                          │ recovery where existing coverage is weakest, but does not establish that insufficient     │
│                          │ relocation caused those errors. This proposal is untested.                                │
