│ patch_description        │ Reducing relocation improved mean offline error from 2.31 to 1.98, supporting a further   │
│                          │ test of spatial preservation. For mild observed deterioration, relocate one of five       │
│                          │ particles instead of two. Keep the three-particle response for stronger deterioration,    │
│                          │ and allow dispersed swarms to retain more particles because they already provide spatial  │
│                          │ coverage.                                                                                 │
│                          │ The hypothesis is that small changes often leave useful particle positions intact: one    │
│                          │ relocated scout can initiate recovery while four particles continue local tracking.       │
│                          │ Preserve memory reevaluation, velocities, and the existing radius rule. Memory refresh    │
│                          │ costs only about 0.4–0.6% of evaluations in the supplied results, providing little budget │
│                          │ motivation for discarding memories. This proposal remains untested; its main risk is      │
│                          │ slower recovery when a small fitness drop masks substantial peak movement.                │
