│ patch_description        │ Capping relocation at three particles previously reduced mean offline error from 2.31 to  │
│                          │ 1.98, although one case benefited from stronger relocation. This suggests testing whether │
│                          │ existing spatial coverage can guide the response.                                         │
│                          │ Preserve at least two particles in every response. Relocate a third particle only when    │
│                          │ deterioration is substantial, recent progress is weak, and the swarm diameter is smaller  │
│                          │ than the relocation region's diameter. Otherwise relocate two particles. The hypothesis   │
│                          │ is that compact, stalled swarms need additional exploration, while dispersed or improving │
│                          │ swarms benefit from retaining more spatial anchors. Keep the radius schedule, memory      │
│                          │ reevaluation, and velocities unchanged to isolate relocation selection. This new gate     │
│                          │ remains untested.                                                                         │
